module test.claim.qualified_pattern_head_witness_test

data qualified_pattern_head_note: String = "A QUALIFIED PATTERN HEAD MUST BIND WHAT THE BARE SPELLING BINDS. Two spellings of one pattern name the same declaration, so they must bind the same node; only the authored string differs. MECHANISM: lookup_variant_in_type forks on whether the head contains a dot. The bare branch answers from the SCRUTINEE, which carries the instantiation. The dotted branch answered from the SYMBOL INDEX, which returns the coproduct's DECLARATION -- uninstantiated -- so the payload bound to the declaration's type PARAMETER instead of the scrutinee's type ARGUMENT, and every field read off the bound value reported no such field on type 'T'. MEASURED, minimal, both arms in one fixture: one generic coproduct, one concrete record, and two probe functions differing only in the spelling of the head. A NON-GENERIC coproduct cannot discriminate this at all -- declaration and instantiation coincide there -- which is why the fixture is generic. THE FIX PRESERVES ADMISSION: the index lookup still runs first and still decides whether the head names a variant of this coproduct at all, so a head naming some other coproduct's variant misses exactly as before. What changes is only where the bound NODE comes from once admission succeeds -- the scrutinee when it carries that variant, the declaration otherwise, which is the pre-existing answer for a scrutinee that does not. ZERO-DRIFT: the added lookup runs only inside the dotted branch, so no bare pattern reaches it, and the fallback arm reproduces the previous answer byte-for-byte. WHY MAIN IS GREEN WITHOUT THIS: the v1 seed closure matches almost exclusively on bare heads, so an ordinary regen exercises the bare branch only -- which is exactly why this witness authors the qualified arm rather than relying on the corpus to contain one. The population that reaches this path grows with the namespace work, where every pattern head is qualified by construction. dissolve-on: never -- permanent regression control for the spelling-identity law in pattern position. IDENTICAL IMPORT LISTS ARE LOAD-BEARING AND WERE NOT AT FIRST. The first revision imported only QualpatResult and QualpatPayload into the qualified probe and all four names into the bare one, because the qualified probe does not NEED the variant names in scope. That made the two arms differ in the import set as well as in the head spelling, so they could differ in source-closure construction, import binding, symbol-index use and cache temperature -- and the floor duly reported the qualified arm at 58800ms CPU against a 5000ms budget with 1.21GB RSS growth while the bare arm passed. That measurement is CONFOUNDED: the arms were a controlled experiment for the SEMANTIC discriminator and not for the COST one, which is the control-independence failure this repository already names -- a control must name its adversary, and cost was an adversary these arms never excluded. Both probes now import all four names, so the only surviving difference is the spelling of the two pattern heads. The semantic RED is unaffected and was re-proven in both directions after the change: on the pre-fix binary the qualified arm returns false and the bare arm returns true; on the post-fix binary both return true. Whether the cost delta survives the corrected control is a question for the hermetic floor, which is the only instrument that can see it -- measured wet, both arms cost 98.7s locally and the delta is simply absent, because the wet corpus load dominates and amortizes whatever the floor pays per claim."

fn w_qualified_pattern_head_binds_the_instantiation() -> Bool {
  compile_dag_rust_emit_check(
    "module qualpat_qual_probe_mod\n\nimport test.fixture.qualpat_provider \{ QualpatResult, QualpatPayload, QualpatOk, QualpatErr \}\n\nfn qualpat_qual_read(r: test.fixture.qualpat_provider.QualpatResult<test.fixture.qualpat_provider.QualpatPayload>) -> String \{\n  match r \{\n    test.fixture.qualpat_provider.QualpatOk \{ value: v \} => v.root\n    test.fixture.qualpat_provider.QualpatErr \{ code: _ \} => \"\"\n  \}\n\}\n",
    "src/qualpat_qual_probe_mod.rs",
    ["fn qualpat_qual_read", ".root"],
    []
  )
}

fn w_bare_pattern_head_is_unchanged() -> Bool {
  compile_dag_rust_emit_check(
    "module qualpat_bare_probe_mod\n\nimport test.fixture.qualpat_provider \{ QualpatResult, QualpatPayload, QualpatOk, QualpatErr \}\n\nfn qualpat_bare_read(r: QualpatResult<QualpatPayload>) -> String \{\n  match r \{\n    QualpatOk \{ value: v \} => v.root\n    QualpatErr \{ code: _ \} => \"\"\n  \}\n\}\n",
    "src/qualpat_bare_probe_mod.rs",
    ["fn qualpat_bare_read", ".root"],
    []
  )
}

test fn qualified_pattern_head_binds_the_instantiation() -> Bool {
  w_qualified_pattern_head_binds_the_instantiation()
}

test fn bare_pattern_head_is_unchanged() -> Bool {
  w_bare_pattern_head_is_unchanged()
}
